// ContentConditionModel One condition on a model request's content — gate #3's counterpart to :class:`ArgConditionModel`,
// with a closed “part“ in place of an argument name since a model request has no tool-defined
// vocabulary to name.
type ContentConditionModel struct {
	// Op How an argument condition compares. A closed set of operators rather than an expression
	// language: a condition is always ``<arg> <op> <value>``, with no composition, precedence or
	// negation for a reader to unpick, which is the property a security control needs and a mini-DSL
	// loses on its second release.
	//
	// ``REGEX`` is the one operator whose *value* is itself expressive. It is here because the
	// conditions operators actually ask for — a ``DROP`` of any table, an ARN outside their own
	// account — are not reachable by glob, and the alternative was authors approximating them with
	// ``contains`` and getting a broader rule than they read. It carries a cost the others do not: a
	// pattern can be slow enough to matter, so it is compiled where it is authored and bounded where it
	// is evaluated (see :func:`_regex_holds`).
	Op ArgOp `json:"op"`

	// Part Which part of an outbound model request a condition reads.
	//
	// A closed set, unlike gate #1's free-form argument name: a tool's arguments are the tool author's
	// vocabulary and we cannot enumerate them, while a model request has a shape every provider shares.
	// Naming the part is what keeps a rule meaning one thing — "no card numbers in what the user sent" and
	// "no card numbers anywhere in the request" are different controls, and a criterion that silently meant
	// the wider one would over-refuse.
	//
	// ``SYSTEM`` is separate from ``MESSAGES`` because the two differ in who wrote them: a system prompt is
	// the operator's own text, message content is whatever reached the agent. A jailbreak rule pointed at
	// everything would fire on the system prompt that describes what to refuse.
	Part  ModelRequestPart `json:"part"`
	Value interface{}      `json:"value,omitempty"`
}

